# Non-Functional Requirements — ${PROJECT_NAME}

> Stability: **stable**. Targets to uphold across all milestones.

## NFR.1 Performance

| Id | Metric | Target | Notes |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| NFR.1.1 | <e.g., LCP on landing page> | < 2.5s | <network profile> |
| NFR.1.2 | <e.g., INP> | < 200ms p75 | typical interactions |
| NFR.1.3 | Initial bundle (if UI) | < 250 KB gzipped | route splitting required |
| NFR.1.4 | <e.g., API p95 latency> | < ... | |

## NFR.2 Reliability

| Id | Requirement |
| :--- | :--- |
| NFR.2.1 | Controlled retry on `5xx`/`429` with exponential backoff, max 3 |
| NFR.2.2 | No double execution of mutations (`Idempotency-Key`) |
| NFR.2.3 | App state recoverable after page refresh |
| NFR.2.4 | Conflicts (HTTP 409) surfaced with refresh suggestion |

## NFR.3 Security

See [`../architecture/SECURITY_AND_AUTH.md`](../architecture/SECURITY_AND_AUTH.md). Binding requirements:

| Id | Requirement |
| :--- | :--- |
| NFR.3.1 | Strict CSP without `'unsafe-inline'`/`'unsafe-eval'` |
| NFR.3.2 | Full security headers (HSTS, X-CTO, Referrer-Policy, Permissions-Policy) |
| NFR.3.3 | No secrets/tokens in `localStorage` long-lived |
| NFR.3.4 | Sanitization of any user-generated HTML rendered |
| NFR.3.5 | Dependency audit on CI; block on `high`/`critical` |
| NFR.3.6 | Login rate-limited; UI shows consistent message |

## NFR.4 Accessibility (if UI)

| Id | Requirement |
| :--- | :--- |
| NFR.4.1 | WCAG 2.1 AA on core pages |
| NFR.4.2 | AAA contrast for body text in dark mode |
| NFR.4.3 | All interactions completable from keyboard |
| NFR.4.4 | Correct ARIA on custom components |
| NFR.4.5 | Focus always visible |
| NFR.4.6 | Automated a11y test in CI |

## NFR.5 Observability

| Id | Requirement |
| :--- | :--- |
| NFR.5.1 | Shared logger with levels |
| NFR.5.2 | W3C `traceparent` propagation across boundary |
| NFR.5.3 | Production telemetry sink configurable via env |
| NFR.5.4 | `correlationId` displayed in user-facing error toasts |
| NFR.5.5 | Build/bundle stats archived in CI artifacts |

## NFR.6 Internationalization

| Id | Requirement |
| :--- | :--- |
| NFR.6.1 | i18n with hierarchical keys `domain.action.target` |
| NFR.6.2 | Dates/numbers/currencies via the canonical locale API |
| NFR.6.3 | User locale persisted on the SSoT |
| NFR.6.4 | Default `${PROJECT_DEFAULT_LOCALE}`, fallback `${PROJECT_FALLBACK_LOCALE}` |
| NFR.6.5 | Pseudo-locale available for CI smoke |

## NFR.7 Maintainability

| Id | Requirement |
| :--- | :--- |
| NFR.7.1 | Strict typing; zero `any` at boundaries |
| NFR.7.2 | Coverage minimum ${COVERAGE_TARGET}% on boundary code and shared utilities |
| NFR.7.3 | Files < 200 lines (soft cap); refactor when exceeded |
| NFR.7.4 | ADR for every significant architectural choice |
| NFR.7.5 | Import alias convention enforced |
| NFR.7.6 | Conventional Commits + PR template with DoD checklist |

## NFR.8 Deployability

| Id | Requirement |
| :--- | :--- |
| NFR.8.1 | Reproducible builds (`ci` install + build) |
| NFR.8.2 | Runtime config via env + `${RUNTIME_CONFIG_ENDPOINT}` |
| NFR.8.3 | Liveness endpoint `/healthz` |
| NFR.8.4 | Cache-busting via hashed asset filenames |
| NFR.8.5 | Simple rollback (immutable artifact per version) |

